// The signed mirror of tests/xfail/lit_wide_past_uint64. A magnitude in (INT64_MAX, UINT64_MAX] is a legal
// `uint64` literal, but under a unary minus it needs a signed type wider than `int64`, and there is none.
// Folded at the minus, so this is a parse error too — the negation is not the destination's business.
fn int32 main() {
    int64 a = -18446744073709551615;
    return 0;
}
